      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Reading the Quipu on the Yupana</h3>In a <i>quipu</i>, numbers are written with knots: each order carries from 0 to 9 knots, and the absence of a knot means zero (<htcite0>). The <i>Yupana</i> is a board used to build those same numbers by placing marks in its rows (<htcite1> ; <htcite2> ; <htcite3>). In this game a quipu appears with one number on each of its cords. Read the knots and set the same number on the Yupana below.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "37c3bba9-4fa7-4fe5-8816-a059e9f73001",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "The Quipu: numbers in order",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "9618a83e-f232-49db-84f6-fc3455a3f1d1",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Drawing to count",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "e92e3d06-886e-4d3c-811f-bcbcce9aa832",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Change of direction (Part I)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6fd2997b-caf1-4620-a58f-1140388ab8c1",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Change of direction (Part II)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p>The <i>\"Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay\"</i> method utilized on this page was developed and published by Dhavit Prem (<htcite0>) of the Yupanki Association (<htcite1>). This method follows the vertical model of <i>Yupana</i>, as presented by Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala (<htcite2>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2d2ea4a5-506b-4dbf-aaa4-3a10a8fbbd9c",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "07",
                        "day": "25"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 354 - 363",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "pp. 361 - 362",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"ArmsAntonio\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('ArmsAntonio', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Image of the book by Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala, published in <htdate0> and shared for free on Archive.org (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
